---
import Breadcrumb from "../components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
import { webPageJsonLd } from "../lib/seo";

const title = "Privacy Notice | Landscaping Calculators";
const description =
  "Privacy notice for these landscaping calculators. Measurements stay in your browser. The site does not set its own cookies, and advertising scripts are not loaded.";
const pathname = "/privacy/";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={webPageJsonLd({ title, description, pathname, breadcrumb: "Privacy" })}>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <Breadcrumb current="Privacy" />
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">How {site.legalName} handles information. Last updated {site.updatedLabel}.</p>
  </header>
  <article class="prose">
    <h2>Who this covers</h2>
    <p>
      This policy describes the free calculators published by {site.publisherName} at this site.
      The public email is on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. There is no company and no
      street address.
    </p>

    <h2>Calculations stay on your device</h2>
    <p>
      The gravel, mulch, topsoil, and sod calculators run in your browser. Lengths, depths,
      densities, and prices you type are used to update the page on your device. The site does not
      have an account system, and it does not receive those numbers as form submissions. The pages
      are static files.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      This version of the site does not set its own cookies and does not load analytics or
      advertising scripts. Boxes labeled Advertisement are empty placeholders with a fixed size.
      They are not ads.
    </p>
    <p>
      If advertising is added later, most likely Google AdSense, this policy will be updated
      before those scripts are enabled. AdSense uses cookies and similar technologies to serve and
      measure ads, including on sites that participate in its program. Google describes that
      processing in the
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a>
      and the
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">advertising technologies page</a>.
      Until this policy says ads are on, they are not.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted on Cloudflare. When your browser requests a page, Cloudflare receives
      ordinary connection data such as your IP address, the user agent, and the URL, and uses it
      to deliver the file and protect the network. That processing is described in the
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.
      We do not run a separate application log of calculator inputs, because those inputs never
      leave your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Messages you send</h2>
    <p>
      If you email {site.contact.email}, the message contains whatever you put in it, along with
      your email address. That note is used to answer you or to correct a figure on the site. It
      is not sold.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The calculators are written for adults ordering landscape material. The site is not directed
      at children under 13, and it does not knowingly collect their personal information.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      When this policy changes, the date at the top of the page will change with it. A change that
      turns on advertising will be made here first, in plain language, not only inside a script.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
